    "m2_prompt_trader_proposal_original": "**Action**: Hold\n\n**Reasoning**: The evidence supports maintaining the current JPM position without directional changes. The technical picture is genuinely mixed: price ($177.33) sits below the 10 EMA ($178.13) and 50 SMA ($178.86) with negative MACD (-1.60), yet the long-term uptrend remains intact at 15% above the 200 SMA. The April 19 bounce occurred on weak volume (13.4M vs 31.5M on the selloff), creating a bearish divergence that undermines the bull's reversal thesis. Critically, Q1 2024 earnings data is unavailable, leaving the fundamental picture incomplete and preventing a high-conviction directional call. The risk-reward at current levels (~1:1 to 1:1.5) is not compelling enough to add, and the downside tail to the 200 SMA ($153.73) if $170 support fails is real. Maintain benchmark weight with a hard stop-loss discipline at $170, and await either a 50 SMA reclaim on above-average volume or the Q1 earnings release as the decisive catalyst.\n\n**Stop Loss**: 170.0\n\n**Position Sizing**: Keep at benchmark weight; do not concentrate beyond standard single-name allocation given elevated volatility (ATR $3.50, realized vol 27.76%)\n\nFINAL TRANSACTION PROPOSAL: **HOLD**",
